cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use insilicoPCR in published work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "insilicoPCR"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Duceppe
    given-names: Marc-Olivier
repository-code: "https://github.com/duceppemo/insilicoPCR"
url: "https://github.com/duceppemo/insilicoPCR"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - in silico PCR
  - qPCR
  - primer validation
  - bioinformatics
  - BLAST
  - genomics
abstract: >-
  Portable desktop and command-line application for in silico PCR against
  genome assemblies (FASTA) and sequencing reads (FASTQ), with realistic
  amplicon calling (primer orientation, product size limits, and weighted
  3'-end mismatch assessment), qPCR probe support, read-level calling and
  read extension for FASTQ input, a check of every input file before the
  run, consolidated TSV and HTML reports, and a synthetic gel visualizer.
